2003016,3],[42008013,42008013,3]],"xn":8}},"people":[{"id":"moses_2108","name":"Moses","also":"","summary":"Drawn (or Egypt. mesu, “son;” hence Rameses, royal son). On the invitation of Pharaoh (Gen. 45:17-25), Jacob and his sons went down into Egypt.","verses":774,"father":"Amram","mother":"Jochebed","v":[1,3,4,10,14,18,19,20,21,27,28,29,30]},{"id":"israel_682","name":"Israel","also":"","summary":"One who follows on another’s heels; supplanter, (Gen. 25:26; 27:36; Hos. 12:2-4), the second born of the twin sons of Isaac by Rebekah. He was born probably at Lahai-roi, when his father was fifty-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[5,22,29,31]},{"id":"abraham_58","name":"Abraham","also":"Abram","summary":"Father of a multitude, son of Terah, named (Gen. 11:27) before his older brothers Nahor and Haran, because he was the heir of the promises. Till the age of seventy, Abram sojourned among his kindred in his native country of Chaldea.","verses":277,"father":"Terah","mother":"","v":[5]},{"id":"isaac_616","name":"Isaac","also":"","summary":"The only son of Abraham by Sarah. He was the longest lived of the three patriarchs (Gen. 21:1-3).","verses":123,"father":"Abraham","mother":"Sarah","v":[5]},{"id":"aaron_1","name":"Aaron","also":"","summary":"The eldest son of Amram and Jochebed, a daughter of Levi (Ex. 6:20). Some explain the name as meaning mountaineer, others mountain of strength, illuminator.","verses":331,"father":"Amram","mother":"Jochebed","v":[14,27,28,29,30]},{"id":"jethro_2431","name":"Jethro","also":"Deuel, Reuel, Raguel","summary":"“The priest of Midian,” Moses’ father-in-law (Ex. 2:18)=Raguel (Num. 10:29).","verses":16,"father":"","mother":"","v":[18]},{"id":"midian_2075","name":"Midian","also":"Midianites, Midianitish","summary":"Strife, the fourth son of Abraham by Keturah, the father of the Midianites (Gen. 25:2; 1 Chr. 1:32).","verses":38,"father":"Abraham","mother":"Keturah","v":[19]},{"id":"pharaoh_2331","name":"Pharaoh","also":"","summary":"The Pharaoh of the Exodus was probably Menephtah I., the fourteenth and eldest surviving son of Rameses II. He resided at Zoan, where he had the various interviews with Moses and Aaron recorded in the book of Exodus.","verses":138,"father":"","mother":"","v":[21,22]},{"id":"zipporah_3095","name":"Zipporah","also":"","summary":"A female bird. Reuel’s daughter, who became the wife of Moses (Ex. 2:21).","verses":3,"father":"Jethro","mother":"","v":[25]}],"places":[{"id":"nile_895","name":"Nile","kind":"Water (River)","lat":19.21141,"lon":30.56733,"summary":"Dark; blue, not found in Scripture, but frequently referred to in the Old Testament under the name of Sihor, i.e., “the black stream” (Isa. 23:3; Jer. 2:18) or simply “the river” (Gen. 41:1; Ex. 1:22, etc.) and the “flood of Egypt” (Amos 8:8).","verses":30,"v":[9]},{"id":"egypt_362","name":"Egypt","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":26.4902,"lon":29.8808,"summary":"The land of the Nile and the pyramids, the oldest kingdom of which we have any record, holds a place of great significance in Scripture.","verses":564,"v":[18,19,20,21]},{"id":"midian_796","name":"Midian","kind":"Region","lat":28.75,"lon":34.75,"summary":"An Arabian tribe descended from Midian. They inhabited principally the desert north of the peninsula of Arabia. The peninsula of Sinai was the pasture-ground for their flocks.","verses":44,"v":[19]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[4872,4872,6030,2005,2005,3808,3808,3808,539,0,3808,8085,6963,6963,6963,3588,559,559,559,3068,3068,3808,3808,7200,413,413],[3068,3068,3068,559,413,4100,4100,4100,3027,3027,3027,4294,4294,559,559],[7993,776,776,776,776,559,559,559,7993,7993,7993,776,776,776,776,1961,1961,1961,5175,5175,4872,4872,5127,6440,6440],[7971,7971,3027,3027,270,270,270,2180,2180,2180,3068,3068,559,413,4872,7971,7971,7971,3027,3027,2388,2388,0,0,1961,1961,1961,1961,4294,4294,4294,3709,3709,3709],[461